    },
    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "Given that $y=-\\frac{\\ln x}{5}$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The derivative of the natural logarithm is the reciprocal function:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\ln x)=\\frac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nWe apply our formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(-\\frac{\\ln x}{5}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\frac{1}{5}\\,\\ln x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\ln x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/id": "8e8e4d74-87ca-5b5c-b102-da0e438f051c",
